if you manually change only the state file from t3 to t2, but your .tf configuration still says t3, Terraform will try to make AWS match the configuration (t3).
Example:
AWS actual:
t3.micro

State file manually changed:
t2.micro

main.tf:
t3.micro

Then: terraform plan

Terraform compares:
Configuration → t3.micro
State          → t2.micro

So it may plan to change the resource to t3.micro to match your configuration.
But there is an important problem
The state file is supposed to represent what Terraform knows about the real AWS resource. 
If you manually edit it to a false value, you can confuse Terraform and cause incorrect plans.
